# wrapscan path allowances — root-relative globs.
# docs/research/ holds verbatim founding-research records: wide markdown
# tables and source URLs that cannot wrap without breaking table syntax or
# mangling quoted material. The house 85-column limit binds everywhere else
# — keep this glob exactly this narrow.
docs/research/**

# docs/sessions/ took over as the session index when atelier's archivecut.py
# retired docs/SESSIONS.md into it (2026-11-20). Each old index entry now sits,
# word for word, near the top of the session file it linked: one deliberately
# long line per entry, and `archivecut.py --verify` rebuilds the retired file
# from them byte for byte, so they cannot be rewrapped. atelier exempts the same
# folder for the same reason. The cost: new session files are no longer
# column-checked at commit time.
docs/sessions/
